# Auto commit & push dev — Mind & Venture (MV2)

After completing substantive work in this repo, **commit and push `dev` without asking**.
Never push `main` by hand: Homebase Daily Ship (05:00) merges dev into main, runs the
selftest, and takes it live (GitHub Pages + itch) only if dev has new commits.

## When to commit

- Game code (`index.html`, `claude/**`, `js/**`, `sw.js`), assets, maps, and player-facing fixes
- Do **not** commit IDE junk (`.vs/`, `DocumentLayout*.json`, `.suo`, backup files)
- Do **not** commit secrets or large binary blobs unrelated to the task
- Do **not** commit unless there are real changes (no empty commits)

## Workflow

1. `git branch --show-current` must say `dev` (`git switch dev` if not)
2. `git status` and `git diff` — stage only files related to the task, by explicit path
3. Write a concise commit message (1–2 sentences, focus on why)
4. `git commit` → `git pull --rebase --autostash origin dev` → `git push origin dev`
5. Tell Paulo: commit hash, and "it's in the Test lab now" (quest screen → The Office → Test lab).
   It goes live at `https://mindandventure.pauloventura.org/` after the next Daily Ship.

Urgent live fix only when Paulo says "ship now" / "push live now":
`powershell -File C:\Users\PVProductions\HOMEBASE\scripts\daily-ship.ps1 -Only MV2`

## Remote

- Repo: `https://github.com/paulooventura/MV2.git`
- Work branch: `dev` · live branch: `main` (Daily Ship only)

## Do not

- Push `main`, force-push, amend pushed commits, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks
- Stage entire `.vs/` folders or unrelated C# Unity experiments unless the user asked for those
